  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43340760",
      "title": "Starting Project & Analyzing Mutation Options",
      "lectureOrder": 166,
      "videoOrder": 154,
      "sourceHash": "2c727d7e8e4b67fc4185fc06881542f3ca4c41cc6837db12e8fcaada882e80ed",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.42,
          "end": 2.67,
          "en": "Now for this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.67,
          "end": 6.75,
          "en": "I prepared a brand new basic NextJS project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.75,
          "end": 8.85,
          "en": "and you find it attached.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.85,
          "end": 10.23,
          "en": "Once you downloaded it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.23,
          "end": 13.11,
          "en": "you'll just need to run npm install once",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.11,
          "end": 15.24,
          "en": "to install all the dependencies,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.24,
          "end": 17.82,
          "en": "and then you can start the development server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.82,
          "end": 19.713,
          "en": "with npm run dev.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.7,
          "end": 24.21,
          "en": "And you'll then get a very simple application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.21,
          "end": 28.62,
          "en": "that allows you to view posts if there were any.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.62,
          "end": 30.63,
          "en": "We'll add some soon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.63,
          "end": 32.31,
          "en": "And which most importantly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.31,
          "end": 35.49,
          "en": "therefore also allows you to add new posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 35.49,
          "end": 39.09,
          "en": "And that's precisely what we'll work on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.09,
          "end": 40.47,
          "en": "throughout this section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 40.47,
          "end": 44.55,
          "en": "because, of course it's that adding posts part",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 44.55,
          "end": 47.28,
          "en": "that involves the creation of new data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.28,
          "end": 49.5,
          "en": "and therefore the mutation of data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 49.5,
          "end": 52.683,
          "en": "and that's exactly the main topic of this section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 53.94,
          "end": 55.35,
          "en": "So we got a form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 55.35,
          "end": 58.74,
          "en": "in this starting application I provided to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 58.74,
          "end": 60.72,
          "en": "And the goal of course, is to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 60.72,
          "end": 62.73,
          "en": "that when this form is submitted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 62.73,
          "end": 65.73,
          "en": "with help of that create post button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 65.73,
          "end": 69.12,
          "en": "that we save the data that has been entered here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 69.12,
          "end": 71.88,
          "en": "that we store the uploaded image somewhere,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 71.88,
          "end": 74.97,
          "en": "and that we store the title and the content somewhere,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 74.97,
          "end": 77.58,
          "en": "for example, in a database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 77.58,
          "end": 82.11,
          "en": "And indeed, in this starting project I prepared for you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 82.11,
          "end": 84.93,
          "en": "you'll find a lib folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 84.93,
          "end": 89.4,
          "en": "and in there, you'll find a posts.js folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 89.4,
          "end": 92.34,
          "en": "which does indeed include code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 92.34,
          "end": 95.703,
          "en": "to store a new post in a database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 96.57,
          "end": 99.50999999999999,
          "en": "And this file actually also contains",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 99.50999999999999,
          "end": 101.52000000000001,
          "en": "much more code than that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 101.52000000000001,
          "end": 106.11,
          "en": "It also includes all the code for setting up that database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 106.11,
          "end": 107.61,
          "en": "and that code will run",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 107.61,
          "end": 109.97999999999999,
          "en": "every time you start this application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 109.97999999999999,
          "end": 113.58,
          "en": "making sure that all the necessary tables are created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 113.58,
          "end": 115.92,
          "en": "if they don't exist already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 115.92,
          "end": 120.27,
          "en": "And as you see here, we have a users table,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 120.27,
          "end": 124.83,
          "en": "we have a posts table, and we have a likes table.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 124.83,
          "end": 127.35,
          "en": "And I'm using a SQLite database here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 127.35,
          "end": 129.99,
          "en": "to store all that table data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 129.99,
          "end": 133.62,
          "en": "And I also got some code here to set up two dummy users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 133.62,
          "end": 135.933,
          "en": "which we'll use throughout this section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 136.8,
          "end": 139.65,
          "en": "You will learn how to add authentication",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 139.65,
          "end": 142.62,
          "en": "and user management later in this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 142.62,
          "end": 146.57999999999998,
          "en": "For now, we'll work with these dummy users here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 146.57999999999998,
          "end": 147.93,
          "en": "So that's what we got in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 147.93,
          "end": 152.16,
          "en": "And then as mentioned, we got this storePost function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 152.16,
          "end": 155.13,
          "en": "which in the end, of course should be triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 155.13,
          "end": 159.48,
          "en": "whenever this form here is submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 159.48,
          "end": 162.42000000000002,
          "en": "And that, of course means that we need to find out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 162.42000000000002,
          "end": 165.84,
          "en": "how we can handle the submission of this form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 165.84,
          "end": 169.38,
          "en": "And for that, we got various options.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 169.38,
          "end": 171.18,
          "en": "One option would be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 171.18,
          "end": 175.82999999999998,
          "en": "to set up a standalone separated backend API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 175.82999999999998,
          "end": 179.76,
          "en": "that accepts requests that contain that form data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 179.76,
          "end": 183.54,
          "en": "and that then stores the submitted data in some database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 183.54,
          "end": 185.88,
          "en": "Kind of similar to what I showed you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 185.88,
          "end": 188.01,
          "en": "in the data fetching section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 188.01,
          "end": 191.883,
          "en": "where we also started with an external API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 192.78,
          "end": 197.61,
          "en": "But for the same reasons we didn't use that external API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 197.61,
          "end": 200.07,
          "en": "in that data fetching section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 200.07,
          "end": 203.73,
          "en": "the reason was in the end that we own the data source",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 203.73,
          "end": 206.04,
          "en": "and therefore it doesn't really make sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 206.04,
          "end": 208.47,
          "en": "to set up such an extra API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 208.47,
          "end": 211.05,
          "en": "For that reason, I won't use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 211.05,
          "end": 214.14,
          "en": "that external API approach here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 214.14,
          "end": 217.82999999999998,
          "en": "because why would we create a separate backend API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 217.82999999999998,
          "end": 219.6,
          "en": "and a separate project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 219.6,
          "end": 222.39,
          "en": "if we can actually integrate the logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 222.39,
          "end": 224.91,
          "en": "for accepting form submissions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 224.91,
          "end": 227.31,
          "en": "and storing data in some database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 227.31,
          "end": 230.223,
          "en": "directly into our NextJS application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 231.12,
          "end": 232.92000000000002,
          "en": "And as it will turn out,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 232.92000000000002,
          "end": 235.82999999999998,
          "en": "we can indeed manage all that directly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 235.82999999999998,
          "end": 238.17000000000002,
          "en": "in this NextJS application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 238.17000000000002,
          "end": 240.75,
          "en": "And that's therefore the approach I'll use here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 240.75,
          "end": 244.11,
          "en": "in this section because this is a NextJS course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 244.11,
          "end": 245.22,
          "en": "and being able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 245.22,
          "end": 249.423,
          "en": "to handle data submissions is a core NextJS feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 250.47,
          "end": 254.4,
          "en": "Now, what we could do as an alternative would be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 254.4,
          "end": 259.4,
          "en": "to add some route handlers here in our project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 259.86,
          "end": 263.91,
          "en": "We could, for example, in the app folder, add an API folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 263.91,
          "end": 266.46,
          "en": "and then there add a posts folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 266.46,
          "end": 267.87,
          "en": "or whatever you wanna name it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 267.87,
          "end": 271.92,
          "en": "And then in there, add a file named route.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 271.92,
          "end": 275.31,
          "en": "I taught you about these route handlers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 275.31,
          "end": 277.74,
          "en": "earlier in the course already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 277.74,
          "end": 281.19,
          "en": "In there, we could export a function called post.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 281.19,
          "end": 284.67,
          "en": "And with that we would be able to send",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 284.67,
          "end": 289.503,
          "en": "and handle post requests to /api/posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 290.7,
          "end": 292.71,
          "en": "And then we could put all the logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 292.71,
          "end": 294.93,
          "en": "for extracting the request body",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 294.93,
          "end": 296.97,
          "en": "because we would receive the request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 296.97,
          "end": 299.19,
          "en": "as a argument automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 299.19,
          "end": 303.06,
          "en": "And all the logic for storing that extracted data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 303.06,
          "end": 306.333,
          "en": "into this function here, into this route handler.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 307.38,
          "end": 308.61,
          "en": "We could do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 308.61,
          "end": 311.25,
          "en": "and that might be a valid approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 311.25,
          "end": 315.09,
          "en": "if we also have other clients submitting data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 315.09,
          "end": 316.92,
          "en": "a mobile app for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 316.92,
          "end": 320.28,
          "en": "that also needs to send data entered by a user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 320.28,
          "end": 323.88,
          "en": "But if we're just building this one NextJS application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 323.88,
          "end": 327.57,
          "en": "this also isn't really something we have to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 327.57,
          "end": 330.21,
          "en": "Sure, we could set up those extra routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 330.21,
          "end": 333.99,
          "en": "and then send data to those routes from the client side,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 333.99,
          "end": 337.44,
          "en": "but NextJS actually offers us a better way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 337.44,
          "end": 341.07,
          "en": "of handling data submissions and data mutations,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 341.07,
          "end": 344.253,
          "en": "and that would be Server Actions.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
